  please cite the software using this metadata.

title: >-
  GRIBS: JSON-Configured Solid Rocket Motor
  Internal-Ballistics Simulator

type: software

version: "0.3.1-alpha"

date-released: "2026-09-18"

authors:
  - family-names: "Kurokawa"
    given-names: "Hikaru"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Team-TSA/GRIBS"

url: "https://github.com/Team-TSA/GRIBS"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - internal ballistics
  - solid rocket motor
  - rocket propulsion
  - thermochemistry
  - NASA CEA
  - numerical simulation
  - Python

abstract: >-
  GRIBS is a JSON-configured solid rocket motor internal-ballistics
  simulator. It includes grain regression, unsteady chamber-pressure
  calculation, nozzle-flow modeling, thrust calculation, optional
  erosive burning, optional throat erosion, and post-burnout blowdown.
  GRIBS supports an external NASA CEA thermochemistry backend and a
  manually configured pressure-dependent property-fit backend.